{#- EVERY WORD THE SITE SAYS, IN EVERY LANGUAGE, AND EVERYTHING ABOUT THOSE
   LANGUAGES — one page (Chase, 2026-09-27: "all language controls can be on
   the page that actually edits the language"). The site's pages and the
   emails and forms, one language at a time.

   ONE FIELD PER LINE, the English above it when the language is not English.
   Not a column per language: that stops working somewhere around four, and
   the site's languages are meant to grow to thirty. The language is a select
   for the same reason.

   WHAT YOU SEE IS WHAT YOU DOWNLOAD. The file for a translator holds the
   lines on screen — a section, a search, "Needs work", or "All" — and the
   button says how many. Choosing lines needs no controls of its own.

   The language's own settings (dev and live switches, default, donation
   form, how it reads, removing it) are one dialog away, because they are set
   once and then left. -#}

<div class="ms-bar c-bar">
  <label class="c-pick">
    <span data-i18n="con.editing">Editing</span>
    <select id="cLang" disabled></select>
  </label>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cLangSet" disabled
          data-i18n="con.langSettings">Language settings</button>
  <span class="c-gap"></span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cDown" hidden></button>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cUp" hidden data-i18n="tl.upload">Upload translation</button>
  <input type="file" id="cFile" accept=".csv,text/csv" hidden
         aria-label="Upload translation" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:tl.upload">
  {#- Always enabled: "nothing has changed" is a claim about the copy this
     page loaded, and the remedy for doubting it is to read again. -#}
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cReload" data-i18n="con.reload">Reload from GitHub</button>
</div>

{#- Shown instead of the editor when GITHUB_TOKEN is absent. -#}
<p class="rolegate" id="cNotConfigured" hidden></p>

<div class="adm-content" id="cRoot" hidden>
  <nav class="c-sections" id="cSections" aria-label="Sections"></nav>
  <div class="c-panel">
    <div class="c-search">
      <input type="search" id="cFind" autocomplete="off"
             placeholder="Find a word or phrase…" aria-label="Find a word or phrase…"
             data-i18n-attr="placeholder:con.find,aria-label:con.find">
      <span class="c-count" id="cCount"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="c-rows" id="cRows"></div>
  </div>
</div>

{#- A returned translation, line by line, in place of the editor until it is
   approved or put away. Lines the checks flag start unticked. -#}
<div class="c-review" id="tlReview" hidden>
  <div class="tl-bar">
    <span class="tl-count" id="tlReviewCount" role="status"></span>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="tlCancel" data-i18n="common.cancel">Cancel</button>
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="tlApprove"></button>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-items" id="tlItems"></div>
</div>

<div class="ms-savebar" id="cSaveBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="cDirtyCount">0 unsaved changes</span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="cSave" data-i18n="con.save">Save</button>
</div>

{#- LANGUAGE SETTINGS, for the language being edited. The console's dialog
   shell, so it looks and closes like every other dialog. Each control saves
   as it is changed, like Settings: one decision, one result. Filled in by
   admin-content.js. -#}
<div class="dlg-back c-set" id="cSet" hidden>
  <div class="dlg c-set-dlg" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="cSetTitle">
    <div class="c-set-head">
      <h3 id="cSetTitle"></h3>
      <button type="button" class="ln-x" id="cSetClose" aria-label="Close" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:con.close">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <div class="c-set-body" id="cSetBody"></div>
  </div>
</div>
